{
  "archive": "wavefunction_overlap.qvf",
  "description": "wavefunction.gto with an AO overlap member, so that the Appendix A.1 normalization contract is checked by every validator: CO with spherical s, p and d shells on C and a spherical s and a Cartesian (pure: false) d shell on O. The overlap diagonal is 1 for every spherical AO and for d_xx, d_yy and d_zz, 1/3 for d_xy, d_xz and d_yz, and for the O s shell, whose contraction is deliberately not normalized, its axial self-overlap 0.660580261291. AO order: C s, C p(m=-1), C p(m=0), C p(m=+1), C d(m=-2), C d(m=-1), C d(m=0), C d(m=+1), C d(m=+2), O s, O d_xx, O d_xy, O d_xz, O d_yy, O d_yz, O d_zz. The MOs are the Lowdin orbitals S^(-1/2), orthonormal in this metric, and the density matrix is that of the seven lowest, doubly occupied (tr(P S) = 14 = basis.n_electrons); illustrative numbers, not a converged calculation.",
